                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.296,
            0.822,
            0.316
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A triangle is the most basic closed shape. As we know, it consists of:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.321,
            0.825,
            0.341
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• three corner points, that we call the vertex of the triangle, and"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.345,
            0.848,
            0.38
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "three line segments or the sides of the triangle that join the pairs of vertices."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.381,
            0.833,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Triangles come in various shapes. Some of them are shown below."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.407,
            0.837,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.163,
                0.407,
                0.837,
                0.576
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_0_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.587,
            0.847,
            0.642
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe the symbol used to denote a triangle and how the triangles are named using their vertices. While naming a triangle, the vertices can come in any order."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.642,
            0.848,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The three sides meeting at the corners give rise to three angles that we call the angles of the triangle. For example, in ∆ABC, these angles are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle CAB , \\angle ABC , \\angle BCA"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " which we simply denote as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { A } ,   \\angle \\mathrm { B }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\complement ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " respectively."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.725,
            0.751,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What happens when the three vertices lie on a straight line?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.781,
            0.497,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.1 Equilateral Triangles"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.816,
            0.848,
            0.873
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Among all the triangles, the equilateral triangles are the most symmetric ones. These are triangles in which all the sides are of equal lengths. Let us try constructing them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.881,
            0.753,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Construct a triangle in which all the sides are of length 4 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.448,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
